The sentence the conjunction rule exists to hold clew to: nobody is asked,
and the sandbox is what keeps that bounded. Reporting this would contradict
the reason `approval_policy` is left out of `bypass-permissions`.

The second file is the other half on its own, in the profile spelling, with
something still asking. Neither file is a finding and neither is the pair,
because Codex reads one configuration rather than both.

>>> .codex/config.toml
approval_policy = "never"
sandbox_mode = "read-only"
>>> nested/.codex/config.toml
approval_policy = "on-request"
default_permissions = ":workspace"
